"body": "# Tile layouts\n\n## Surfaces\n\n| Source | Tiled area |\n|---|---|\n| A floor plan room | The floor, less cabinets, tubs, showers and appliances (tile runs under a toilet) |\n| A floor plan wall side | The wall, less doors, windows, openings and blocks against it |\n| A framing wall | The inside or outside face, less doors and windows |\n| A typed outline | The outline as typed |\n\n- A layout follows its source. If the source is deleted, the layout keeps its last outline and says so.\n- Walls take a height range, for example a backsplash from 36\" to 54\".\n- Areas are added or cut out on the tile page and stay in place on the source.\n\n## Patterns\n\n| Pattern | Tile size |\n|---|---|\n| Straight grid | Width and height, any rotation |\n| Running bond | Offset of 1/2 or 1/3 of a tile |\n| Herringbone | The long side is the width |\n| Basketweave | The long side is the width |\n| Hexagon | Width across the flats |\n| Versailles | The small square; four sizes in each module |\n\n## Start and cuts\n\n- The layout starts from the middle of the area, a corner or a picked point, with a joint or the middle of a tile on it.\n- Balanced cuts try a joint and a tile middle on each direction and keep the layout with the fewest thin cuts.\n- The smallest cut is 1/3 of a tile unless set. Thinner cuts are shown in red.\n- The page shows the starting tile and the chalk lines, dimensioned from the walls.\n\n## Reports\n\n| Report | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| Tile cut list | Each cut's size and shape, equal cuts grouped, straight cuts taken from offcuts where they fit |\n| Tile order | Full and cut tiles, tiles to order with waste (10%, or 15% for diagonal and herringbone), boxes, grout and thinset estimates |\n"
